data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The utility classes don't define font-size-3xl. The tokens don't have --font-size-3xl either. So the inline style `fontSize: 'var(--font-size-3xl)'` will result in invalid/no font-size. The greeting will probably render at default browser size. This is a bug relative to the design - I asked for \"large, bold type size\" but didn't specify a token. However, the developer used a non-existent token. I should either fix it or send it back. But the design didn't explicitly specify the font-size token, so this is somewhat my fault. But the developer should have checked the catalog/tokens.\n\nSince I can merge and fix minor issues myself? No, the orchestrator brief says \"Where an agent returns work that misses the design, send it back once with the exact failure. Where it still misses, report that as unmet.\" But also \"Check the developer's work yourself first. Run fetch, merge what comes back, build it, and look at the result.\"\n\nThe design says \"Rendered in a large, bold type size.\" The developer chose --font-size-3xl which doesn't exist. This is a miss - the greeting won't be large. I should send it back with the exact failure. But before that, let me build it and verify. Actually, since I already see the token doesn't exist, I can send it back now. But I should also verify the build works.\n\nActually, wait - maybe I should just fix it myself? The orchestrator doesn't write application code. I should send it back. But sending it back will cost time. The design says large, bold type size but doesn't specify the exact token. The developer could have used --font-size-xl or --font-size-prose-h1. I think --font-size-prose-h1 (2rem) would be good, or we could use a larger size. Actually there's no 3xl. The largest available is --font-size-xl (1.5rem) or --font-size-prose-h1 (2rem). \n\nHmm, I need to decide: send back for this one issue, or accept and fix by telling qa? No, I must not write code. But I can decide the design should be more specific. Actually, the easiest path: accept the work with a note that the font-size token is missing, but then the greeting won't be large. The qa will catch this as \"does not match design\". Better to send back now.\n\nLet me first build it to confirm the build succeeds and see what else might be wrong. Then I'll send back if needed.\n\nActually, before building, I need to install dependencies. Let me do npm install."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789849182,"id":"chatcmpl-b7f4875f4a6a41678caad7d86c2f8425","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

